        "displayName": "WebdriverIO 8 Web",
        "readme": "<p>This module demonstrates Serenity/JS web testing capabilities using the legacy WebdriverIO v8 as the browser automation tool.</p>\n<h2>Why this module?</h2>\n<p>WebdriverIO v8 remains in use by teams that haven&#39;t yet migrated to v9. Serenity/JS maintains backward compatibility to ensure existing test suites continue to work without modification.</p>\n<h2>Features demonstrated</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>PageElement interactions via the <code>@serenity-js/web</code> abstraction layer</li>\n<li>WebDriver and DevTools protocol support</li>\n<li>BrowseTheWebWithWebdriverIO ability implementation for v8</li>\n<li>Same portable web specs as Playwright and WebdriverIO v9</li>\n</ul>\n"
